.TH QTAR 1 "September 2026" "Qore tar 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qtar \- create, inspect and extract archives with Qore
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qtar
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.I archive
.RI [ files ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qtar
provides archive operations using Qore's tar module and libarchive.
Compression is detected from the archive extension when creating an archive,
unless selected explicitly. Supported methods include gzip, bzip2, xz,
zstd and lz4. OpenSSL supplies the encryption implementation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create (c)
Create an archive from files or directories.
.TP
.B extract (x)
Extract archive contents. Use \-C to select the destination directory.
.TP
.B list (t)
List archive contents. Use \-l for the detailed listing.
.TP
.B add (a)
Add files to an existing archive.
.TP
.B info (i)
Show archive metadata.
.TP
.B encrypt (e), decrypt (d)
Encrypt or decrypt an archive using AES-256-CBC.
.TP
.B cat
Write one archive entry to standard output.
.TP
.B verify
Verify archive integrity.
.TP
.B diff
Compare an archive with a directory or another archive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help. After a command, show its specific options.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
qtar create backup.tar.gz project/
qtar extract backup.tar.gz \-C restore/
qtar list \-l backup.tar.gz
qtar cat backup.tar.gz project/README
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qore (1),
.BR tar (1)
.PP
The qore-tar-module-doc package provides the complete API references.
